Usage: mockserver [-hV] [COMMAND]
MockServer — mock, proxy & record HTTP(S), gRPC, and more.
  -h, --help      Show this help message and exit.
  -V, --version   Print version information and exit.
Commands:
  run      Start MockServer (default subcommand).
  ui       Start MockServer and open the dashboard UI in a browser.
  proxy    Start MockServer in port-forwarding (proxy) mode.
  openapi  Start MockServer and initialize expectations from an OpenAPI spec.
  import   Load expectations from a JSON file into a running MockServer.
  lint     Check expectation JSON files for expectations that can never match
             or will not match as written. Advisory: nothing is changed, and no
             server is needed.
  demo     Start MockServer pre-loaded with a small set of example expectations
             and print a getting-started URL and sample curl.
  version  Print MockServer version and exit.
  help     Display help information about the specified command.

Examples:
  mockserver run -p 1080
  mockserver ui -p 1080
  mockserver proxy --to https://api.example.com
  mockserver openapi ./petstore.yaml -p 1080
  mockserver import ./expectations.json -p 1080
  mockserver lint ./expectations.json
  mockserver demo -p 1080
  mockserver -p 1080

Legacy flags (-serverPort, -proxyRemotePort, -proxyRemoteHost, -logLevel) are
supported for backward compatibility.
